<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo in $15 mln China express bus j/v.</title>
<headline>Daewoo in $15 mln China express bus j/v.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daewoo Corp, a unit of Daewoo Group, said on Tuesday it had agreed with Tianjin Long-distance Bus Co to set up a $15 million express bus joint venture in Tianjin, China.</p>
<p>The joint venture company, named Tianjin Jinwoo Transportation Co Ltd, would start operation in August with 50 deluxe express buses. The company would have a paid-in capital of $10 million and seek annual sales of $9 million.</p>
<p>The two companies would each have a 50 percent stake in the venture. --Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
